  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Site Office",
    "overview": "ZimEstimate looks like a well-run site office: a midnight-navy board on the wall, brass labels on it, and clean white worksheets on the desk where the numbers live. The navy frame (top bar, home hero, closing band, footer, phone bottom bar) carries the brand. Inside it, the work happens on pale, flat worksheets with thin rules, one blue for every action, and colour that only appears when something has a real status.\n\nApp screens are calm and exact. Cards sit flat on a pale blue-grey board, separated by 1px rules rather than shadows, and the figures, units and status do the talking. Marketing surfaces (the home page) can be bolder in composition, but they stay in the same two worlds: navy with gold, and the pale worksheet. The phone is the main screen, so every decision is checked at about 375px first.\n\nSettled by the owner (16 Nov 2026): the product is light-themed only, with no dark mode, and it uses no line-art illustrations. The home page is flat, quiet navy with no glow or grid lines.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "A midnight-navy frame around pale, flat worksheets.",
      "Brass gold appears only on navy (eyebrows, labels, icon fills); on light surfaces gold becomes a deep ink.",
      "One action blue per page for buttons, links, arrows and selection.",
      "Green, amber and red only for real status.",
      "Sora for headings, Instrument Sans for reading, IBM Plex Mono for eyebrows and figures that need to line up.",
      "Phone-first, with a fixed navy bottom bar on mobile."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Blue Rule",
        "body": "A page has one interactive colour, Action Blue (with its deep and link variants). Never colour buttons or categories per type.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Gold Lives on Navy Rule",
        "body": "Brass Gold is only used on Midnight or Steel Navy. On light surfaces, use Gold Ink or Selected Surface instead.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Icon Tile Rule",
        "body": "Since 22 Nov 2026, every decorative icon sits on the same tile: steel-navy outline with a soft gold duotone fill on a pale blue-grey tile with a thin edge (the `--icon-tile-*` tokens, the `.icon-tile` class, `EstimateIcon.module.css`). Only icons that show status use status colours: done green, in progress blue, not started grey, a warning amber, Log out and Danger zone red.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Status Is Earned Rule",
        "body": "Green, amber and red mean saved/OK, needs attention and failed. They never decorate.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Status Scheme Rule",
        "body": "Since 21 Nov 2026, every status pill in the app uses the same mapping: in progress is the pale info-blue wash (Info Wash fill, Link Blue text), complete/purchased is green, draft, pending and not started are grey (mist fill, Ink Secondary text), over-purchased or failed is red, and amber only for something that needs action. The info-blue wash is a status tint, not an action, so it does not break the One Blue Rule. Waiting to buy is grey, never amber.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Figures Line Up Rule",
        "body": "Money, quantities and units use tabular numerals, so columns of figures align.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Worksheet Rule",
        "body": "Cards sit flat at rest, separated by Rule Light borders. A hover or selection changes the border to Action Blue; it doesn't add a shadow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Navy Sheet Rule",
        "body": "Since 22 Nov 2026 (owner), every phone pop-up (the \"+\" sheet, More, the project \u22ee menu, Share, Invite, Log purchase, filters, the marketplace detail sheet) is a navy sheet: white title, muted navy-ink copy, content as light cards or rows on it, one blue main button, focus rings in gold. Settings (all widths) and the New BOQ builder (phones) sit on the navy page too. Light and dark will follow the device setting (`docs/tasks/system-dark-mode.md`); sheets stay navy in both.",
        "section": "colors"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep app screens light: Site Board page, Worksheet cards, 1px rules.",
      "**Do** use Action Blue for every interactive element on a page, and only Action Blue.",
      "**Do** put Brass Gold on navy only, and switch to Gold Ink on light surfaces.",
      "**Do** use tabular numerals for money and quantities.",
      "**Do** design at about 375px first, with 44px touch targets, and clear the mobile bottom bar.",
      "**Do** use Phosphor duotone icons (navy outline, gold fill, pale tile) on choice and start cards."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** add a dark theme. The owner rejected it on 16 Nov 2026.",
      "**Don't** add line-art illustrations, including on empty states, errors and contractor pages.",
      "**Don't** add glows, gradients or grid lines to the navy home sections; they stay flat and quiet.",
      "**Don't** give categories or item types their own colours.",
      "**Don't** use green, amber or red for decoration.",
      "**Don't** lift cards with shadows at rest.",
      "**Don't** put duotone icons in data tables."
    ]
  }
}
